- Human Bingo — Bingo card with prompts (e.g., “has a sibling,” “volunteers”) — people mingle to fill rows. Great for larger groups, 10–20 min. Encourages conversation.  
- Two Truths and a Lie — Each person states two true things + one lie; group guesses the lie. Small/medium groups, 10–20 min. Fun and personal.  
- Compliment / Appreciation Circle — Everyone says one welcoming compliment or what they appreciate about the school/event. Small/medium groups, 10–15 min. Sets a warm tone.  
- Speed Networking (rotating pairs) — Short timed chats with prompts (e.g., “best childhood memory”). Works for any size with time control, 15–30 min. Good for building connections.  
